  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing the Database Class**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `AppDatabase` class and how to seed it with useful test data. I\'m considering initial tests and making things easier to work with. I need to make sure the database is not too large. I am considering pre-configured test data, and how to include that in the creation.\n\n\n**Defining Initial Data**\n\nI\'ve decided on the initial data for my application. I need to include an admin user for the initial launch, so I\'ll add \"admin\" with PIN \"1234\". I also have a list of categories and a pre-populated set of standard medical tests with their associated categories and prices. I\'m adding a phlebotomist user too: \"amit\" with PIN \"0000\".\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the Room database class `/app/src/main/java/com/example/data/local/AppDatabase.kt`. It handles schema declarations, callbacks for prepping initial test configurations, and default user profiles."
