    thinking: "**Defining App States**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the application\'s states and navigation structure, specifically the application flow. I\'m starting with the initial screens, including a dynamic splash screen transition. Next is the login screen, with role-based access for admins or phlebotomists. Username saving and offline login support are important considerations.\n\n\n**Designing App Structure**\n\nI\'ve transitioned to sketching out the core application screens: Dashboard with key metrics, New Patient Entry form with comprehensive fields, Test Management for admin and phlebotomist roles, Reports with admin-focused data, and Settings for configuration. I can confirm, I can build all this in Compose. I am planning to model a reactive state structure using a centralized `LabViewModel` for seamless navigation and global state management.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create a translation system in `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/translation/Translations.kt` to support real-time language toggling between English and Gujarati. Field phlebotomists can translate the entire application natively with a simple one-click header button."
